shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.short_desc=Manage waypoints
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.1=The waypoints command lets you manage Baritone waypoints.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.2=Waypoints mark locations for later use. Each waypoint has a tag and an optional name.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.3=The info, delete, and goal commands can specify waypoints by tag. If a tag has multiple waypoints, you can select the specific one.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.4=When save has no arguments, it uses the USER tag, an empty name, and your current position.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.usage=Usage:
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.list=> wp [l/list] - List all waypoints.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.list_tag=> wp <l/list> <tag> - List waypoints by tag.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.save_default=> wp <s/save> - Save an unnamed USER waypoint at your current position.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.save=> wp <s/save> [tag] [name] [pos] - Save a waypoint with the specified tag, name, and position.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.info=> wp <i/info/show> <tag/name> - Show waypoint information by tag or name.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.delete=> wp <d/delete> <tag/name> - Delete a waypoint by tag or name.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.restore=> wp <restore> <n> - Restore the last n deleted waypoints.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.clear=> wp <c/clear> <tag> - Delete all waypoints with the specified tag.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.goal=> wp <g/goal> <tag/name> - Set a waypoint as the goal.
shadowbaritone.command.waypoints.long_desc.example.goto=> wp <goto> <tag/name> - Set a waypoint as the goal and start pathing.
